content.text:
Much better on mobile: topbar fits (pips, timer, REQ 329, ×1, sound, pause), feed messages readable, minimap bottom-right compact, selection panel + command card don't overlap the minimap... though the command card "FIELD COMMAND / Select a unit or building." is partially clipped by the minimap? Looking closely: "Select a unit or building." text is cut off on the right edge — the command card is centered (left: 50% transform) with max-width 44vw; its text wraps... it says max-width 44vw but the card still extends under minimap? The cc is centered — at 390px wide, center card spanning ~172px wide, text "Select a unit or building." wraps to two lines and gets clipped? The image shows "Select a unit or building." with the final period possibly clipped at right edge of card. Actually the card seems to run under the minimap (minimap overlaps it). The command card is centered at 50% with width fitting content up to 44vw=172px — but its content (the hint text) might force wider via white-space? .cc-hint has no nowrap. Hmm, looking at the image again: the "FIELD COMMAND" title and "Select a unit or building." — the text touches the minimap's left edge and appears slightly clipped by it. The minimap is at right:6px width 108px → occupies ~276-384px; command card centered ~97-291px? No overlap then... but visually the card's right edge is behind the minimap. The card is horizontally centered; its content "Select a unit or building." is one long line wider than 44vw? max-width constrains card but inline content wraps normally... unless the .cc-hint has white-space normal (default) — it wraps. Then card width = up to 44vw=172px, text wraps to 3 lines — but screenshot shows single line truncated — because .cc-hint? Let me just make the mobile card smaller: hide the hint entirely on ≤860px and shrink card to fit content; also move the card left of minimap: set left: 6px, transform none, bottom: 6px, and selection panel above it? That stacks two panels on left — crowded but works:

Better mobile layout:
- #selection-panel: left:6px bottom:6px (as now)
- #command-card: left:6px, bottom: 64px (above selection panel), transform none, width max-content
- #minimap-wrap unchanged bottom-right

That avoids all overlap. Let me apply: 

@media (max-width: 860px) {
  #command-card { left: 6px; transform: none; bottom: 60px; max-width: 46vw; }
  .cc-hint { display: none; }  /* keep footprint tiny when nothing selected */
}

When nothing selected, card shows only "FIELD COMMAND" title — fine.

Also the topbar REQ shows "+5.0/s" green income hidden — fine (req-side hidden).

Timer "14:58" good. Apply CSS tweaks.

